## 2026-11-01T20:28Z - Claude Fable 5.1 (as this session reports itself)
- The node restructured to categories (Julian): GRAPHICS, SPEECH, MUSIC, STORE are the devices; CMD and EVENTS the one conversation (80 OPEN names the service / profile; SPEECH 85 TARGET picks SSA1 / DKTRONIC / VOTRAX); a category's folders (GRAPHICS/V9990, V9938, ZXNEXT, MD, PINATIVE; MUSIC/MP3, 8BIT, 4BIT, SID, AY38912, VGM, FM, MOD, MIDI, GME) are store paths - a SAVE is PUT GRAPHICS/V9990/PATTERNS, a LOAD is GET, read from the normalized path UniDOS gives (DE: a count then 11-char names; MakeTag). An installer preloads assets; a game then only sends commands and reads events - and a new type is a folder here and a player on the Pi, no ROM change. The Pi: vdp.js loads a profile's installed assets (GRAPHICS/<profile>/PATTERNS, TILES, LAYER2, PALETTE) at OPEN; audio.js plays MUSIC/<type>/ by its folder (mpg123, aplay raw, sidplayfp, vgmplay, adplay, xmp, fluidsynth, mpv's gme; ERR noplayer when the player isn't installed; .MID GM / GS / XG, XG rendered as GM). Pi tests: vdp.js 29, audio.js 19, all pass. The node's test (streamer_test.py) is rewritten for the categories; the structure passes (CheckDrive, the root files, GRAPHICS:CMD, the vdp commands, EVENTS, the asset PUT and GET, SPEECH's three targets, MUSIC) but the Pi-side folder CAT (ExamineNext over a LIST) still has bugs and the root listing repeats one entry - to finish. The ROM assembles.
